Subject: AOT: Layer B typed regions

What this does
  AOT: Layer B typed regions.

Why we need it
  A typed loop region keeps the counter, accumulator and temporaries unboxed across the whole body.

What it adds
  `qjsaot` emits a region for a call-free, top-tested loop with an unconditional back-edge: values are carried as `(double, isint)` pairs and boxed only at an exit/deopt, property reads use a hoisted shape guard, array reads use a dense-array + `bound <= len` guard, keeps it as an exact int64-range double with no per-iteration FITSI (the exact `qjs_aot_fitsi` rule is re-applied at every box site), and elides the IV-keyed index check. New engine helpers: `qjs_aot_fitsi`, `box_num`, `to_num`, `dense`, `elem_num`, `field_guard`, `field_read`, `get_length_num`, `var_ref_ptr`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
